            <ArticleTitle>Severe acute necrotizing pancreatitis associated with lipoprotein lipase deficiency in childhood.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1407-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>An 11-year-old girl with lipoprotein lipase deficiency experienced recurring episodes of abdominal pain. She initially underwent appendectomy for suspected appendicitis; however, the appendix was normal. Pancreatitis was subsequently identified as the cause of her pain.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
